package cosmonic:minimal-agent;

// The four cosmonic:agent@0.3.0 interfaces this agent calls, and nothing else.
//
// The published `cosmonic:agent/agent` world also imports `tools`. A component
// that imports an interface must have it bound when it is deployed, so
// including that world would make every workload running this example declare
// a tools provider it never calls. Naming the imports keeps the manifest, and
// the list of capabilities an operator reviews, down to what the code uses.
//
// wasi:http/handler@0.3.0 is exported through the `wasip3` crate, which
// carries its own WIT, so it is not named here.
world minimal-agent {
  import cosmonic:agent/inference-types@0.3.0;
  import cosmonic:agent/models@0.3.0;
  import cosmonic:agent/chat@0.3.0;
  import cosmonic:agent/session@0.3.0;
}
